# Markdown Formatting

Use Prettier + markdownlint. Run `pnpm format` (or format the open file) before committing docs.

## Tooling (source of truth)

- Prettier override for `*.md` / `*.mdx`: `tabWidth: 2`, `proseWrap: "preserve"`, `printWidth: 100`
- Project config: [.prettierrc](mdc:.prettierrc), [.markdownlint.json](mdc:.markdownlint.json)

## DO

- Align markdown tables with Prettier (pipe tables OK)
- Use fenced code blocks with an explicit language (`bash`, `ts`, `sql`, `json`, `text`)
- Put ASCII diagrams / directory trees in ` ```text ` fences (never ` ```md `)
- Keep list nesting at 2-space indents (Prettier markdown default here)
- Prefer `**bold**` / `*italic*` (asterisk style)
- End files with a single trailing newline

## DON'T

- Do **not** wrap prose aggressively (`proseWrap` stays `preserve`)
- Do **not** use ` ```md ` for non-markdown samples — Prettier will reformat nested markdown and destroy trees/diagrams
- Do **not** leave decorative emphasis like `****` or invalid bold markers; use real `**text**` or remove them
- Do **not** hand-edit generated docs that are in [.prettierignore](mdc:.prettierignore)

```text
# ✅ DO: diagram in a text fence
gemini-proxy/
├── apps/
│   └── web/
└── packages/
```

```md
# ❌ DON'T: diagram in an md fence (Prettier mangles indentation)
gemini-proxy/
├── apps/
│   └── web/
```

## Tables

```markdown
| Variable       | Description        |
| -------------- | ------------------ |
| `SUPABASE_URL` | Supabase project URL |
```

## Checklist before commit

1. `pnpm exec prettier --check "**/*.{md,mdx}"` (or `pnpm format`)
2. Spot-check ASCII trees still look correct
3. No escaped junk like `\*\*\*\*` in prose
